  m_text: "Did you know that back then people used primitive means to disinfect letters?
    They used to dip them in vinegar, burn them, or pour chemicals like sulphur on
    them. There was even disinfection by slitting. You can see some letters that
    have gone through such processes and have survived to this day from the personal
    collection of Judge Giovanni Bonello in the gallery once you\u2019ve unlocked
    all the locations.\nSee also: <link=https://www.um.edu.mt/library/oar/handle/123456789/81974><u><color=blue>Link</link></u></color>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: b61e9963be7a5634385e0be0327cdfcd, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 5366484808827389454, guid: b61e9963be7a5634385e0be0327cdfcd, type: 2}
